{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 623 days before the 2018 shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D7"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Diltiazem hydrochloride is not on FDA's current shortage list as of 2026-10-21; FDA's history shows an earlier shortage first posted on 2018-02-21, since resolved.",
      "cites": ["D14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The 2018 shortage posting listed Hospira, Inc., a Pfizer Company, with status To Be Discontinued for package NDC 0409-4350-03.",
      "cites": ["E24"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our 100 mg injection vials at both Corvale General and Corvale East carry NDC 00409435003 and labeler Hospira, Inc., matching the discontinued product.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 976095 at Hospira, Inc. (FEI 1925262) ended 2016-06-08 and was classified OAI, 623 days before the 2018-02-21 shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D7", "E11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Warning Letter was issued to the same plant on 2017-02-14, 372 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D8", "E16"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later FDA inspection 1064827 at the plant ended 2018-08-15 and was classified OAI, 175 days after the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D11", "E13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to transfer 50 vials of 100 mg from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would raise Corvale East from 9.3 to 14 days on hand while Corvale General remains above two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D15"]
    }
  ]
}
